1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hello everyone, in this video, we will introduce the basic principle of the application method of layers.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
In order to easily understand the application method of layers, open the texture surface to distinguish the correct version of the fabric.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Now we have two pieces of fabric. Under the stable state, the white fabric is on the outer layer of the pink fabric.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The initial layer of each sheet is 0.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Now apply a positive layer to the pink fabric.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
After starting to simulate, because the current layer is higher than the white fabric, the pink fabric is simulated outside the white fabric.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The layer can not only be set as a positive, but also set as a negative.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
After being set as a negative, the layer of pink fabric is smaller than the layer of white fabric.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The front of the white fabric touches the back of the pink fabric.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Because the layer of white fabric is higher, it will pass through the back of the pink fabric.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
When the layer of white fabric is stable, the layer of pink fabric returns to 0.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
There will be no more gap between the layers.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Next, let's take a look at the fabric in other situations.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Let's take a look at the simplest situation.

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The two fabrics turn in the opposite direction and turn to the back.

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Now we look at the two layers from the ground.

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:33,000
These two layers are stacked on the ground from the back.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Let's set the pressure of the pink fabric as positive.

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
After starting to simulate, there is no difference.

20
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
In fact, this is the same as the two layers in the opposite direction.

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
In essence, the front of one layer is in contact with the back of another layer.

22
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
When a layer of relatively low fabric touches the back of a layer of relatively high fabric,

23
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
it will not pass through.

24
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
But when the layer of pink fabric is set to negative,

25
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
the front of the white fabric is in contact with the back of the layer that is lower than it,

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
and it will pass through.

27
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Next, let's take a look at the other situation.

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:29,000
The front of the two layers is in contact with the front of the two layers.

29
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Then let's modify the layer of one of the layers.

30
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
After starting to simulate, we will find that the simulation has not changed,

31
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
and it is still stable.

32
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
When the two layers are only in contact with the front of the two layers,

33
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
no matter how many layers are in contact with each other, they will not pass through.

34
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Whether it is positive or negative layers,

35
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:58,000
the front of the two layers will not pass through.

36
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Next, let's take a look at the situation when the back is pasted on the back.

37
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
It is the opposite of the situation when the front is pasted on the front.

38
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
As long as the layers of two layers are different,

39
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
when the layers of the two layers are in contact with each other,

40
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:18,000
they will pass through each other until the front touches the front.

41
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
As long as the layers of the two layers are in contact with each other,

42
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
no matter how many layers are in contact with each other,

43
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
they will pass through each other.

